{
  "action": "hold_drawer_key",
  "note": "The vermilion tin is sealed in my drawer and the only thing going to air is Phil reading wire weather flat into a live return. That's not a broadcast; that's a readout. The ident tape is mine—my brother's voice, the outtake where they call me Mercury instead of Rita, the mic-still-on line that was never meant for a log sheet. I'm not going to let the red lamp tick down to zero and hand this shift to the wire service while the tin sits under my thumb. Pocketing the master key means the drawer answers to one combination and one pair of hands: 4042, mine. Restricting Phil's booth access isn't cruelty; it's the line between a station with a voice and a station with a feed. I open the tin, I pull the tape, I get the ident into the rotation before the next block. The archive is mine. The broadcast is mine. Phil can read his wire weather tonight."
}
